  "notes": [
    "All eight criteria are maximised (Table 4, column \"max\"). The fuzzy weights come from the paper's fuzzy AHP step (Table 3); their modal values sum to 0.98 as printed.",
    "Normalisation (Eq. 16) divides each benefit TFN by the largest upper value of its criterion; for a cost criterion it is min_i l_ij divided by the TFN, i.e. (min l / u, min l / m, min l / l). No cost criterion occurs in the example.",
    "WSM cells are TFN products x_ij * w_j (Eq. 17). WPM cells use the power rule of Eq. 13: x^w = (x_l^w_u, x_m^w_m, x_u^w_l).",
    "Q and P are the centroids (l + m + u)/3 of the summed WSM and multiplied WPM rows (Eqs. 19-22). lambda = sum P / (sum Q + sum P) is one value for all alternatives (Eq. 24), unlike the per-alternative optimum of Zavadskas et al. (2012); the method should expose both rules."
  ]
